  "serverSectionHasError": "Has an error",
  "helpAntiDpiTitle": "Anti-DPI",
  "helpAntiDpiBody": "The provider's filter reads the server name in the first packet of a TLS connection. Anti-DPI sends that packet so the filter can't parse it while the server receives it as usual. HTTP/2 only.",
  "helpAntiDpiModesTitle": "Methods",
  "helpAntiDpiModesBody": "Basic - the packet goes out in two pieces with a pause.\n1, 2, 3 - ByeDPI techniques: an \"urgent\" (OOB) byte the server drops, and a piece with TTL 1 that is lost at the first router and then resent by the system. The filter sees the packet incomplete or out of order.\nAuto - tries 1, 2, 3 in turn and remembers what worked on this network.",
  "helpAntiDpiCustomTitle": "Custom string",
  "helpAntiDpiCustomBody": "Space-separated parts, in order:\n-s N - a plain split after byte N;\n-o N - a split with an \"urgent\" byte;\n-d N - the piece up to byte N goes out with TTL 1.\nN counts from the packet start, from its end if negative, from the server name with +s (or +h).\nExamples: \"-o1+s -d3+s\" is method 3, \"-d7\" is method 2, \"-s1 -d3+s\".\nNot allowed: -r (the server rejects such a packet) and -o without a -d after it (the server stalls). ByeDPI syntax, but only these three techniques.",
  "helpTlsProfileTitle": "TLS fingerprint",
  "helpTlsProfileBody": "Which app the connection looks like during the handshake. Best is your default browser: the filter then sees one fingerprint from your address. Don't change it needlessly: a change during a block can extend the address \"freeze\".",
  "helpRuExitTitle": "Russian exit",
  "helpRoutingTitle": "Routing",
  "helpRoutingBody": "The routing profile decides which sites go through the VPN and which go directly.",
  "helpDnsTitle": "DNS and IPv6",
  "helpDnsBody": "DNS servers - where DNS queries go inside the tunnel; empty means the default server. IPv6 - whether IPv6 traffic goes through the server.",
  "helpKeyTitle": "Key data",
  "helpKeyBody": "This comes from the key link or subscription: server address and port, the domain from its certificate, login and password. Usually left alone: if a key stops working, add the link again. A custom certificate is only for a server with a self-signed one.",
  "helpExpertTitle": "For experts",
  "h2PaddingLabel": "Size masking (HTTP/2)",
  "h2PaddingDescription": "The first packets of a connection get random padding. HTTP/2 only",
  "blockQuicLabel": "Turn off QUIC",
  "blockQuicDescription": "UDP to port 443 is refused: browsers and apps fall back to TCP inside the tunnel",
  "helpExpertBody": "Protocol - HTTP/2 (TCP) or HTTP/3 (QUIC); anti-DPI works with HTTP/2 only.\nCustom SNI - the server name shown in the handshake instead of the domain; the server must accept it.\nSize masking - the first eight HTTP/2 frames of each connection get 0-255 random bytes (the PADDED flag, part of HTTP/2; the server accepts it as is). The sizes of the tunnel's first requests then differ every time, which makes the VPN harder to recognise. Costs a little traffic; off by default.\nClient Random - a tag at the start of the handshake random the server recognizes the client by. Set only when the admin says so.",
  "antiDpiAutoFailedTitle": "Couldn't get through",
  "antiDpiAutoFailedBody": "Mrrr... I tried all three techniques and none reached the server. Try another server or send a report - it shows where it got stuck.",
  "ruExitLabel": "Russian exit (for trips abroad)",
  "ruExitDescription": "This server is in Russia. Only Russian sites and apps (banks, government services, marketplaces) go through it, everything else directly. Don't turn it on for everyday use in Russia: it does the opposite",
  "ruExitPromptTitle": "Is this server in Russia?",
  "ruExitPromptBody": "\"{name}\" seems to be in Russia. Is it a key for trips abroad? Then only Russian sites and apps (banks, government services, marketplaces) go through it, everything else directly.\n\nIf you are in Russia and this is a regular VPN, pick \"No\". You can change it in the server settings.",
  "ruExitPromptYes": "Yes, for trips",
  "ruExitPromptNo": "No, regular",
  "@ruExitPromptBody": {"placeholders": {"name": {"type": "String"}}},
