  "whatsNewTitle": "What's new in {version}",
  "whatsNewBody": "• Your own anti-DPI string in ByeDPI syntax, checked as you type, with ready-made examples. Server settings → Censorship bypass → Technique\n• TLS fingerprint: the connection looks like your default browser\n• The server page is split into sections, each with a \"?\" explanation\n• If a server's address gets frozen, I no longer knock on it every second: I pause, tell you what's wrong and offer another server\n• For experts: size masking of the first packets (HTTP/2)\n• Settings → How the connection works: what happens step by step\n• For experts: \"Turn off QUIC\" - browsers and YouTube go over TCP inside the tunnel\n• On Android, links and subscriptions now apply everything they set: Russian exit, technique, fingerprint\n• The VPN no longer reconnects when you open the app, and switching servers connects once",
